---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const SITE = 'https://precisionsolutionstech.com';
const title = 'TrailSift for Android Privacy Policy | Precision Solutions Tech';
const description =
  'How TrailSift for Android handles your trail camera photos. Everything runs on your device; the app has no internet permission and your photos are never uploaded.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/` },
      {
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: 3,
        name: 'TrailSift for Android',
        item: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/trailsift-android/`,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'TrailSift for Android Privacy Policy',
    url: `${SITE}/legal/privacy/trailsift-android/`,
    description,
    dateModified: '2026-10-25',
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'Precision Solutions Tech', url: `${SITE}/` },
  },
];
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/legal/privacy/trailsift-android/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li>TrailSift for Android</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>TrailSift for Android Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: October 25, 2026</p>
      <p class="lead">
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>TrailSift</strong> (“we”, “us”) handles information
        when you use the TrailSift app for Android (the “App”), published by
        <strong>Precision Solutions Tech</strong>, operated by <strong>SG TECHNOLOGY LLC</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="summary">Short version</h2>
      <p>
        TrailSift works <strong>on your device, with no signal needed</strong>. It reads the memory
        cards you open, looks for animals with on-device models, and keeps the photos you choose in the
        App. Nothing is uploaded to us. We operate no account system and no servers that receive your
        data. The App does not have Android’s internet permission, so it cannot send anything over the
        network itself.
      </p>

      <h2 id="local">What the App processes on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Photos and videos on memory cards or folders you open, and the information inside them
          (capture time, camera model, the date and temperature stamp printed on the photo)
        </li>
        <li>Results of on-device detection, species identification, stamp reading, and photo sharpness</li>
        <li>The cameras, tags, buck names, and notes you add</li>
        <li>Your settings, and the location (country and US state) you set for each camera</li>
        <li>GPS coordinates some cameras write into their photos, used only to find the camera’s location</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All of this stays on your device. Photos you import are stored in the App’s private storage and
        are included in your device backup like other app data, if you have backups turned on.
      </p>

      <h2 id="location">Location</h2>
      <p>
        Each camera has a location (a country, and a state in the US) that tells TrailSift which
        animals can live there, and optionally a spot rounded to about 1 km. If you tap “Use my current
        location”, the App asks Android for your approximate position once, turns it into a country and
        state using a map stored inside the App, and saves the country, state and rounded spot with the
        camera. Your exact position is not stored. A camera’s spot can also come from GPS written into
        its photos or coordinates you type in, and can be cleared at any time. The App does not track
        your location in the background. You can pick a location from a list instead, or deny the
        location permission.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cards">Memory cards</h2>
      <p>
        When you open an SD card, Android shows its own folder picker and gives the App access only to
        the folder you choose, while you work with that card. The App does not read other folders or
        your photo gallery.
      </p>

      <h2 id="gallery">Saving to your gallery</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose “Save to gallery”, the App adds copies of the photos or videos you picked to your
        device’s Pictures or Movies folder, in a TrailSift folder. The App does not read the rest of
        your gallery.
      </p>

      <h2 id="purchases">Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        The one-time unlock is sold through Google Play. Google handles payment; we do not receive your
        payment details or Google Account information. The App checks your purchase with the Google
        Play app on your device.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The App contains <strong>no analytics SDKs, no advertising SDKs, and no third-party
        trackers</strong>. We do not profile you, and we do not sell or share personal information. The
        App reads date and temperature stamps with Google’s on-device text recognition (ML Kit); because
        the App has no internet permission, that component cannot send anything either. If any of this
        changes, this policy will be updated before the change ships.
      </p>

      <h2 id="network">Network access</h2>
      <p>
        The App has no internet permission. Scanning, importing, tagging, insights, and clearing cards
        all happen on your device. Purchases go through the Google Play app.
      </p>

      <h2 id="people">Photos of people</h2>
      <p>
        Trail cameras sometimes photograph people. TrailSift labels them so you can find them; it does
        not identify who they are. You are responsible for how you keep and share such photos.
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Your library stays on your device until you delete photos, use “Erase all TrailSift data” in
        Settings, or uninstall the App. If you contact support, we keep your message as long as needed
        to help you.
      </p>

      <h2 id="children">Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>The App is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age in your jurisdiction).</p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy. The “Last updated” date will change when we do.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions:
        <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/legal/privacy/trailsift-ios/">TrailSift for iPhone &amp; iPad privacy policy</a>
        ·
        <a href="/legal/privacy/">Company privacy policy</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
